{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The short stainless wood screws fit my recent fastening and mounting work and could serve smaller jobs than my longer construction screws.",
    "The original epoxy felt useful for small repairs alongside that work, where fastening alone might not solve the problem."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Marine epoxy, hose clamps and electrical connectors require specific repair needs that my recent activity does not establish.",
    "The calipers address precision measurement needs I have not shown, and the large washers do not match hardware I currently need.",
    "Duct tape could be useful, but an eighteen-roll pack is more than I would choose for my current work."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Buying construction fasteners seems to have been taken as interest in almost any workshop or repair supply.",
    "Shared materials such as stainless steel do not make items useful to me when their purpose or dimensions do not fit my task."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated nail and wood-screw purchases point most clearly toward fastening and mounting tasks, rather than wiring, hose repairs or precision measurement.",
    "The intended use, dimensions and pack quantity matter to whether I can use an item now; a broadly related tool or supply is not enough."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my fastening and repair interests but extended them to specialized tasks and quantities I have no current need for."
}"}
